{
  "title": "Ingredient parser: amounts and sizes left in the item that curated aliases paper over",
  "description": "Several lines still put part of the amount, a size or a packing word into the item. \
Curated aliases in ramekin-core/src/catalog/data/curated.json key on that exact text, so nutrition works, but each variant needs its own alias and the shopping list shows the junk name. \
Fixture lines (ramekin-core/tests/fixtures/ingredient_parsing): \"1/2 lb. two US sticks unsalted butter\" -> item \"two US sticks unsalted butter\" (a count word plus a stick unit); \"3 6-ounce containers fresh raspberries\" -> \"6-ounce containers fresh raspberries\" (a sized container unit); \"1 3-4 inch chunk of ginger\" -> \"3-4 inch chunk of ginger\"; \"1/2 of a small or 1/4 of a large white onion\" -> \"small or 1/4 of a large white onion\"; \"14 ounces (400 grams) or approximately 4 plain pork sausages (...), casings removed\" -> \"or approximately 4 plain pork sausages\" (an \"or approximately N\" count alternative); \"1 large orange or 2 small ones, juiced\" keeps \"or 2 small ones\" in the item because \"orange\" is read as a color before \"or N\"; and leading \"packed\" (\"packed dark-brown sugar\"), \"good quality\" (\"good quality dark chocolate\") and \"small handful\" (\"handful picked fresh rosemary leaves\") stay in the item. \
After each fix, add an alias for the clean name if it doesn't resolve, then run make catalog-clean-aliases to drop the old key. \
Expect intentional data/ diffs from make pipeline.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "bug",
